  38:     Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
  39: 
  40:     Input structure:
  41:     - Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
  42:     - Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
  43:     - A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
  44: 
  45:     Rule:
  46:     - Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
  47:     - On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
  48:     - Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
  49:     - If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
  50: 
  51:     Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
